<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Central Asia and the Steppe</p><h1 class="st-title">Tashkent Hakimate</h1><p class="st-meta">1784 CE – 1808 CE (approx.) · capital Tashkent</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived city-state centred on Tashkent, built by Yunus Khoja on the Kazakh trade frontier before Kokand absorbed it.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In the 18th century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tashkent">Tashkent</a> was divided into four quarters under rival leaders and passed under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazakhs">Kazakh</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dzungars">Dzungar</a> overlordship. Around 1784 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yunus-khoja">Yunus Khoja</a>, hakim of one quarter, united the city and threw off the authority of the Kazakh khans of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/senior-juz">Senior Juz</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yunus-khoja">Yunus Khoja</a> ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tashkent">Tashkent</a> as an independent state, extending control over nearby towns and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazakhs">Kazakh</a> pastures and trading with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, which welcomed the caravans. He built a strong army and fought the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/khanate-of-kokand">Khanate of Kokand</a>, defeating its forces in 1799.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yunus-khoja">Yunus Khoja</a> died around 1803, and his sons quarrelled. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alim-khan-of-kokand">Alim Khan</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/khanate-of-kokand">Khanate of Kokand</a> conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tashkent">Tashkent</a> in 1808 or 1809, after which it remained a Kokandi city until the Russian conquest of 1865.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 1784 CE – 1808 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path